.TH OMO 1 "August 2026" "omo" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
omo \- ops tools in one terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B omo
.br
.B omo secrets
.I command
.RI [ args ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B omo
is a local TUI host for ops plugins (Docker, Kubernetes, Redis, Git, and others).
With no arguments it starts the terminal UI.
.PP
Credentials live in a KeePass database under
.I ~/.omo/
and are never sent to a remote service.
Plugins run out-of-process over RPC.
.SH OPTIONS
.B omo
takes no flags.
The only subcommand is
.BR secrets .
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B omo
Launch the TUI.
.TP
.B omo secrets list [prefix]
List secret entry paths, optionally filtered by prefix.
.TP
.BI "omo secrets get " path
Print one entry as JSON.
.TP
.BI "omo secrets put " path " [" flags ]
Create or update an entry. Only supplied flags are written.
.TP
.BI "omo secrets delete " path
Remove an entry.
.TP
.B omo secrets reset [--yes]
Delete
.I ~/.omo/secrets/omo.kdbx
(the key file is kept). Recreated on next open.
.PP
Secret paths use
.IR plugin / environment / name
(for example
.BR redis/production/cache ).
.PP
Flags for
.B put :
.BR --username ,
.BR --password ,
.BR --url ,
.BR --notes ,
.BR --attr " key=value"
(repeatable).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B OMO_SECRETS_RESET
If set to
.BR 1 ,
delete the KeePass database before the next open (same as
.BR "omo secrets reset" ).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.omo/keys/omo.key
Vault key. Back this up; without it the database cannot be opened.
.TP
.I ~/.omo/secrets/omo.kdbx
KeePass database.
.TP
.I ~/.omo/plugins/
Installed plugin binaries.
.TP
.I ~/.omo/theme
Saved TUI theme id.
.TP
.I ~/.omo/logs/omo.log
Host log.
.SH KEYBINDINGS
While the plugins list is focused:
.BR D
dashboard,
.BR p
package manager,
.BR i
settings,
.BR t
themes,
.BR r
refresh plugins.
.PP
Inside a plugin:
.B Ctrl+t
switch target,
.B /
filter,
.B ?
help,
.B Esc
back.
.B Tab
cycles focus.
.SH SEE ALSO
KeePassXC(1)
